      "message": "I think this is the safest approach.\n\nI had been wondering whether we could leave has_async_transaction set to true after we selected the thread; if another transaction to the node comes in, it would be added to node-\u003easync_todo, and would still automatically be picked up. This would save you the more complex logic in L2940-L2957 above. \n\nBut, I haven\u0027t totally convinced myself this is safe. There was always some period in time where node-\u003ehas_async_transaction \u003d true without there being any work on the workqueue for it; but previously, that would only be while holding the node lock, and now we drop the node lock in-between.\n\nIf you agree then I think your CL as is is the safest way to go.",
